module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.AffineBaseChangeChart
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.IdealPullbackGenerators
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.PullbackIdealChartGeneration

/-!
# Projecting an ideal through an affine morphism, as subsheaves of the direct image

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf
site `B`, let `F` be an `𝒪_Y`-module on the small étale site of `Y` and let `I ⊆ 𝒪_X` be a
sheaf of ideals on the small étale site of `X`.  Stacks 0GF8 compares the two subsheaves

`I · f_*F` and `f_*((f⁻¹I) · F)`

of the direct image `f_*F`.  This file carries the comparison as an inequality and an equality
of `SheafOfModules.Submodule`s, rather than as a membership statement over each chart.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pushforwardSubmodule` is the direct image of a submodule of `F`
  along a representable morphism, as a submodule of `f_*F`: its sections over an étale chart
  `Q` of `X` are the sections of the submodule over the base-changed chart `Q ×_X Y`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSmul_le_pushforwardSubmodule`: the inclusion
  `I · f_*F ⊆ f_*((f⁻¹I) · F)`, for any representable morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pushforwardSubmodule_le_idealSmul`: the opposite inclusion for an
  affine morphism, granted the chart generation of the inverse-image ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isChartGeneratedPullbackIdeal_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts`: that
  chart generation holds for a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSmul_pushforward_eq` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealSmul_pushforward_eq_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`: **Stacks 0GF8**,
  the equality `I · f_*F = f_*((f⁻¹I) · F)` for an affine morphism and quasi-coherent `I`
  and `F`.

## Implementation notes

The direct image of modules used is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.smallBaseChangeModulePushforward`, the direct image along small-chart
base change of Stacks 03G2, part (4); the sections of `f_*F` over an étale chart `Q` of `X`
are by construction the sections of `F` over `Q ×_X Y`, with the `𝒪_X(Q)`-action restricted
along the structure map `f♯` of Stacks 03G8.  That is what makes
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pushforwardSubmodule` a submodule objectwise with no transport; that
its membership is *local*, which is the sheaf condition a
`SheafOfModules.Submodule` carries, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.coverPreserving_smallBaseChange`.

The inverse-image ideal is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackIdealSubsheaf`, the smallest sheaf
of ideals of `𝒪_Y` containing the pullbacks `f♯(a)` of the sections of `I`; the two products
are `Stacks.Sites.idealSmul`, the smallest submodule with local membership containing the
objectwise products.

Affineness enters only in the opposite inclusion, through two facts: that the base change
`Q ×_X Y` of an affine chart is an affine chart
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAffine_smallBaseChange_obj`), and that over an affine chart `V` of
`Y` lying over a base-changed affine chart the objectwise inverse-image ideal is already
generated by the sections pulled back from that one chart of `X`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.pullbackChartIdeal_le_map`, which is where quasi-coherence of `I` is
used).  The named predicate
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsChartGeneratedPullbackIdeal` isolates the second of these, since
the descent argument of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_idealSmul_pushforward_of_mem_idealSmul_pullbackIdealSubsheaf`
consumes it in that shape.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GF8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GF8)
